design\releases\0_0_3\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md:15:Move the complete action runner to Electron. Electron resolves a persisted action by stable id, prepares its worktree when requested, executes command or agent actions, orchestrates `onBefore`/main/`on`/`onAfter`, streams phase-specific events, and supports cancellation.
design\releases\0_0_3\release_notes.md:6:- Manage linked worktrees from the project configuration.
design\releases\0_0_3\release_notes.md:7:- Assign worktrees to cards and choose a worktree from the action popup.
design\releases\0_0_3\release_notes.md:8:- Commit, update, and integrate assigned worktrees from a card.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:14:User can select the active worktree from the action popup. When the action popup is associated to a card, it reflects the worktree of that card (and also updates it). When the action popup is for the project agent, then the user can select the worktree on which to run the agent project wide.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:18:- The popup header contains the action selector, expand, and close controls in one row; it has no worktree control.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:19:- Card worktree assignments are stored in frontmatter and included in card action contexts. The project-agent context has no worktree assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:20:- Electron uses a card's valid assignment only when an action has `needsWorkTree`. It rejects project contexts for such actions; actions without `needsWorkTree` run in the primary worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:24:- Add an accessible worktree icon/menu at the upper left, on the same row as the right-aligned expand and close buttons. Move the action selector to a second row.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:25:- List only valid linked worktrees reported by Git, plus an unassigned option. Keep invalid card assignments visible with their existing error.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:27:- Disable linked worktrees reserved by another active card. Background cards do not reserve worktrees.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:28:- Before persisting a card assignment, Electron creates a title-slug branch in the selected clean worktree from the opened project branch. Existing branches and dirty worktrees fail without changing the assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:30:- Project context can select any valid linked worktree, including one reserved by an active card, and does not prepare a branch.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:31:- Use the effective assignment for action filtering, prompt preparation, and execution. Electron resolves it only when `needsWorkTree` is true, accepting card or project context; missing, invalid, or unavailable assignments fail before process start. Actions without `needsWorkTree` still run in the primary worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:37:- Card popup shows and updates the card's worktree assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:38:- Card popup disables worktrees reserved by another active card and prepares the selected worktree before saving.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:39:- Project-agent popup keeps one worktree assignment for the current opened-project session and does not persist it.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:40:- An action with `needsWorkTree` runs in the valid worktree supplied by its card or the project agent.
design\releases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:42:- An action without `needsWorkTree` runs in the primary worktree regardless of the displayed assignment.
design\releases\0_0_4\release_notes.md:7:- Use dedicated placeholders for project, worktree, and release folders.
design\releases\0_0_4\release_notes.md:8:- See integrated worktree changes in card commit history.
design\releases\0_0_4\release_notes.md:12:- See worktree status update immediately after integration.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-7-electron-local-folder-project-mode.md:24:- Repository validation only checks for a `.git` directory, which rejects valid Git worktrees where `.git` is a file and does not normalize a nested selection to its repository root.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-7-electron-local-folder-project-mode.md:42:- The selected folder is a Git worktree: accept it even when `.git` is a file.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-7-electron-local-folder-project-mode.md:50:- Add Git service tests for repository-root normalization, nested selections, worktrees, non-repositories and detached `HEAD`.
