design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:3:title: Git worktrees
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:15:Allow Electron to manage linked Git worktrees, assign cards to them, run `needsWorkTree` actions in the assigned worktree, and show worktree/agent state on each card.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:19:- **Primary worktree**: the repository folder currently opened by Electron. It is not necessarily a branch named `main`.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:20:- **Linked worktree**: another folder created through `git worktree add`.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:21:- **Card worktree**: the linked worktree assigned to a card.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:22:- **Parking branch**: an MD²-owned `md2/parking/*` branch that keeps an unassigned linked worktree at the opened project branch commit.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:23:- Git worktrees share one object database but normally check out different branches.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:24:- One linked worktree can be reserved by only one active card. Background cards do not reserve worktrees.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:25:- Project-agent session assignments can use any linked worktree, including one reserved by a card.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:26:- Config can create and remove linked worktrees. Removing one deletes its checkout folder but retains its branch and commits.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:27:- Action execution only uses linked worktrees reported by Git; it never creates one.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:32:- The implemented action model uses `runIn: "project" | "card"` and can automatically transfer successful project-worktree changes to a card worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:39:- Load linked worktrees directly from `git worktree list --porcelain`; do not persist a separate MD² worktree registry.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:40:- Exclude the currently opened primary worktree from the linked-worktree list.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:41:- Git list position is identity: the first linked folder is worktree `1`, the second is `2`, and so on.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:42:- Store a card's one-based worktree index in frontmatter as `worktree: <number>`. A missing field means no assigned linked worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:44:- Detached, locked, and prunable worktrees remain visible with their exact invalid state.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:48:- Show the worktree list in Config > Project as an Electron-only control.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:50:- `+` opens an Electron folder picker, runs `git worktree add <folder>`, and switches the checkout to its MD² parking branch.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:51:- Removing an entry requires confirmation and runs non-forced `git worktree remove`; Git rejects dirty or locked worktrees.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:57:- Show the stored one-based worktree index and allow assignment to Primary/unassigned or any valid linked worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:58:- Disable worktrees reserved by another active card. The card's current assignment remains available to itself.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:60:- Reuse the current card branch even when dirty. A dirty worktree on another branch blocks assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:61:- For a clean worktree, switch to an existing card branch or create it from the opened project branch, then persist the assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:62:- An assigned card selector shows Primary, Commit, Update worktree, and Integrate into project instead of other linked-worktree choices.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:63:- Commit stages all worktree changes. Update flushes pending project saves, checkpoints remaining primary-worktree changes, and rebases the worktree onto the opened project branch. Integrate performs the same project checkpoint, rebases when needed, and fast-forwards the opened project branch to the worktree branch.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:64:- Returning to Primary parks a synchronized worktree before clearing the assignment. Dirty worktrees require Commit & integrate or explicit destructive discard.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:65:- Card indicators and menu availability use the same project-to-worktree comparison. Up means dirty or ahead of the project branch; down means pending project saves or behind the project branch. Upstream state is handled by project-level synchronization.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:66:- Background cards do not reserve their stored worktree. Project-agent assignment does not use card reservations and does not prepare a branch.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:75:- When `needsWorkTree` is true and a card already has a valid assigned worktree, run in that worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:77:- Resolve the card's one-based worktree value against Git's current linked-worktree list and reject missing, invalid, or unavailable entries with the exact validation error.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:78:- Resolve `{{rootProjectFolder}}`, file paths, agent logs, action history, and diff metadata against the prepared execution worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:79:- The renderer sends only action id, context, and run-specific input. Electron reloads the definition, resolves `needsWorkTree`, and validates the selected worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:81:- Selector-time card worktree preparation only selects or creates the card branch.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:82:- Action execution resolves the prepared assignment but never creates, removes, assigns, or prepares a worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:86:- A detached, locked, or prunable worktree reports its exact invalid state.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:87:- Adding or removing a worktree can shift list indices; cards retain their stored values.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:88:- A dirty worktree on another branch blocks preparation and shows the Git error.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:89:- A card branch checked out by another linked worktree remains a Git error.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:90:- Update and integration reject unresolved dirty linked-worktree state. Remaining primary-worktree changes receive a local checkpoint commit before synchronization.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:92:- Concurrent assignment attempts cannot reserve the same worktree for two active cards.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:93:- An unassigned card or non-card context cannot run an action that requires a worktree.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:94:- Card rename or move retains its worktree assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:95:- Worktree update and integration report their own process result. Action completion adds no implicit cross-worktree transfer.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:99:- Add Git integration tests using temporary repositories and real `git worktree add`: discovery, creation, removal, branch retention, assignment, and detached worktrees.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:101:- Add card/data tests for worktree frontmatter, assignment, invalid states and agent-state decoration.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:104:- Add regression tests proving action completion performs no automatic commit, push, merge, cherry-pick, or cross-worktree transfer.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:109:- Electron users can add, view, and remove linked worktrees from Config > Project.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:110:- Active cards cannot select a worktree reserved by another active card; background cards release their reservation.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:111:- Successful card assignment reuses its id/title branch or creates it from the opened project branch before persisting the worktree index.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:112:- Dirty worktrees on another branch fail without changing the card assignment; dirty worktrees already on the card branch are reused.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:113:- Returning to Primary resolves dirty changes and restores the linked worktree parking branch before clearing the assignment.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:116:- Git is the sole worktree source; card assignments use one-based indices from Git's current linked-worktree order.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:119:- Actions with `needsWorkTree` use the card's valid assigned worktree and reject missing assignments or non-card contexts.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:120:- Action execution does not create, remove, or assign worktrees.
design\releases\0_0_3\F-46-git-worktrees.md:122:- Action completion never performs automatic commit, update, integration, or cross-worktree transfer.
